# Copy this file to .env to enable conversational analytics / the Composer /
# the sandbox coding agent (all off by default), and/or to point the app at
# a real S3 bucket instead of the local demo emulator. See README.md's
# "Conversational analytics" section for exactly what the LLM settings below
# send to the provider once set.
#
# .env is gitignored and is read by both ways of running the app: docker
# compose loads it, and app/config.py loads it for ./run.sh and a bare
# uvicorn. (The test suite deliberately ignores it, so a real key sitting
# here can't change what a test run sees.) A real environment variable always
# wins over a value here, so `CI_LLM_MODEL=gpt-5 ./run.sh` overrides one line
# without editing the file — which also means a forgotten `export` from an
# earlier experiment silently outranks the line you write here. Startup lists
# any setting shadowed that way by name; `unset CI_LLM_API_KEY` clears one.
#
# Values are literal to *this* loader — no shell expansion — so a key
# containing $, #, spaces or backticks needs no escaping under ./run.sh.
# Docker compose parses this file itself and does interpolate $, so a key
# containing one is safest exported in your shell (or checked against the
# key fingerprint the app prints on startup). Quotes around a value are
# optional and are stripped. Format: KEY=value, one per line, # for comments.
#
# Any OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible endpoint works: set a URL and a key.
# Leave CI_LLM_BASE_URL unset for Anthropic's own API.

# The API key for whichever endpoint below. Required to turn the LLM features
# on (the one exception is native AWS Bedrock, which signs with an IAM role).
CI_LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional: the endpoint. Its host decides the wire format — see
# CI_LLM_PROVIDER below to override that guess.
#   OpenAI            https://api.openai.com/v1
#   Azure OpenAI      https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1/
#   Azure via gateway https://<gateway-host>/azure-openai  (+ CI_LLM_API_VERSION)
#   AWS Bedrock       https://bedrock-runtime.<region>.amazonaws.com/openai/v1
#   OpenRouter        https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   local (Ollama)    http://localhost:11434/v1
# CI_LLM_BASE_URL=

# The model to use — must be one the endpoint above actually serves.
# CI_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional: the models a user can pick per conversation. Defaults to just
# CI_LLM_MODEL unless that is one of the built-in Claude ids.
# CI_LLM_MODEL_CHOICES=gpt-4o,gpt-5,o3

# Optional: which of those models *can* be asked for extended thinking /
# reasoning — a capability list, since a model that doesn't support it
# rejects the whole request. Whether to ask is the THINKING toggle in the
# CHAT / COMPOSER / modelling-panel headers; this decides where that toggle
# is offered at all, so `none` removes it everywhere (the escape hatch for a
# gateway that rejects the parameter). Leaving it blank is not the same
# thing — blank means "use the default".
# CI_LLM_THINKING_MODELS=gpt-5,o3
# CI_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# Optional: the state that toggle starts in — on unless set to false/0/no/off.
# Turn it off to make thinking opt-in per conversation instead of opt-out.
# CI_LLM_THINKING_DEFAULT=true

# Optional: on the OpenAI wire, max_completion_tokens is one budget covering
# the model's reasoning *and* its answer, so this much headroom is added on
# top of the answer size each feature asks for. Too little and a reasoning
# model spends the lot thinking and never calls a tool ("the model used its
# whole token budget before calling a tool"); raise it, or ask for less
# reasoning with CI_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low.
# CI_LLM_REASONING_TOKENS=8192

# Optional: force the wire format when the URL can't imply it — an
# Anthropic-compatible gateway on a neutral host, or native AWS Bedrock,
# which signs requests with the standard AWS credential chain (IAM role, env
# vars, SSO profile) instead of an API key.
#   auto (default) | anthropic | openai | azure | bedrock
# CI_LLM_PROVIDER=auto
# CI_LLM_AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Azure's older dated API surface, where the deployment name lives in the URL
# path. Setting this also *implies* CI_LLM_PROVIDER=azure on any host, which
# is what makes a corporate gateway fronting Azure work — its hostname says
# nothing about Azure, so nothing else could give it away. Set
# CI_LLM_BASE_URL to whatever a working example passes as `azure_endpoint`
# (the bare resource root, or the gateway's Azure path); the SDK appends
# /openai/deployments/<model>/... itself, so don't include that part. Azure's
# newer /openai/v1/ endpoint needs no version and none of this.
# CI_LLM_API_VERSION=2024-10-21

# Optional: read a different file instead of ./.env, or set it empty to read
# no file at all and take settings from the environment only.
# CI_ENV_FILE=/etc/lazy-bi/env

# Optional: point at a real S3 bucket (or MinIO/LocalStack) instead of the
# embedded demo emulator. CI_S3_ENDPOINT's presence, not its value, is what
# disables the emulator — see app/config.py and the README's "Open
# http://127.0.0.1:8080" section for what happens on first connect (the
# bucket is created if missing, and seeded with demo data if empty).
# CI_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
# CI_BUCKET=cash-intel
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Recommended once CI_S3_ENDPOINT is set above and you're authenticating as
# yourself (rather than a service): a ~/.aws/config profile name, including
# one backed by AWS SSO (`aws configure sso`) — see the AWS CLI's
# "sso-configure-profile-token-auto-sso" guide. boto3 is asked for that
# profile's credentials fresh on every S3 call, so a short-lived SSO
# credential just keeps working — boto3 re-derives it from the (much
# longer-lived) cached SSO token itself, the same way `aws s3 ls --profile
# ...` would, refreshing automatically without ever sitting in this file.
# Takes priority over AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/etc. below when both are set.
# AWS_PROFILE=

# Static fallback used when AWS_PROFILE above is unset — the demo emulator's
# dummy "testing"/"testing" credentials otherwise. A long-lived IAM user's
# access key + secret work with nothing further.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Optional, only alongside the static keys above (not AWS_PROFILE, which
# refreshes its own) and only for a temporary/STS credential pasted in
# directly. An access key starting ASIA... is temporary and *requires* its
# paired token; used alone it fails as InvalidAccessKeyId, not a
# token-specific error, since AWS can't recognize the key at all without it.
# Note this value itself still expires and won't refresh sitting in a file —
# AWS_PROFILE above is the better fit for anything SSO-derived.
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# ── Object-store read cache (app/engine.py) ───────────────────────────────
# Only worth touching when the app points at a real S3 endpoint rather than
# the bundled emulator. See README.md's "Against a real object store" section.

# How stale a query's answer may be, in seconds. Until an entry expires a
# query can answer from bytes read this long ago. 60 suits data that lands
# continuously; raise it well past that (600+) when data lands hourly or
# nightly, which is where the biggest wins are. 0 disables source caching
# entirely and restores the old read-everything-every-time behaviour.
# CI_SOURCE_CACHE_TTL=60

# Largest source, measured in the object store, that gets held in memory as a
# whole frame instead of being streamed per query. Checked before reading, so
# a bigger source is never downloaded just to find out it was too big.
# CI_SOURCE_CACHE_MAX_BYTES=16777216

# Second guard, applied after decoding: compressed columnar data can pass the
# gate above and still expand several-fold in memory. Anything past this is
# dropped again rather than retained.
# CI_SOURCE_CACHE_MAX_RESIDENT_BYTES=268435456

# How long a resolved source *schema* is trusted. Schemas only change when
# someone rewrites the data with different columns, and a model/bundle edit
# clears the cache anyway, so this is only guarding against a change made
# outside the app.
# CI_SCHEMA_CACHE_TTL=300

# How long a spine dimension's min/max date bounds are trusted. Unlike a
# schema these move as rows land, hence the shorter default.
# CI_BOUNDS_CACHE_TTL=120
